---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import CryptoConverter from '@/components/tools/reference/CryptoConverter.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="crypto-converter">
  <CryptoConverter client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the crypto converter works</h2>
    <p>
      The crypto converter has one price per day for each coin, in US dollars. To convert a coin to
      another coin, it divides the two dollar prices. To convert to euros, pounds or another currency,
      it uses the daily euro reference rates of the European Central Bank:
      <code>price in GBP = price in USD × (GBP per EUR) / (USD per EUR)</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      A daily price is a snapshot. Crypto markets trade all the time, and exchanges quote slightly
      different prices, so a trade gives a different amount. Use the result to check an amount or a
      past price, not to time a trade.
    </p>
    <h2>Crypto price history</h2>
    <p>
      The chart shows the daily dollar price of the coin in the conversion since March 2024. A day
      without a snapshot, or with a price far from the days around it, is left out. Move the pointer
      over the chart, or focus it and use the arrow keys, to read the price of a day.
    </p>
    <h2>Stablecoins</h2>
    <p>
      Tether (USDT) and USD Coin (USDC) aim to stay at one US dollar. Their daily price shows how close
      they stayed.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
